kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K2 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.2, 4): the GPU's own buffers.
Page tables on demand: step 13's pool of 16 serves steps 13-22 as before; beyond it a page of tables
is made when needed, zeroed and cleaned to memory before an entry leads to it, and freed with the
pool after the streams are unrouted (KG_UNDO_TABLES, pushed with the pool); at most 1024 tables (2
GB of 4K pages); entries written are cleaned page by page (dirty). GPU addresses for buffers from
kgsl's user range 0x40_0000_0000-0x80_0000_0000, first fit in 64K grains, each buffer followed by
one unmapped grain. redwood_gpu_address/_address_free/_map/_mapped/_unmap are now real: a map enters
one 4K page of the user range (AP[1] for the 2D/3D engines, AP[2] for read-only), _mapped cleans the
dirty table pages and has context 0 drop ASID 0 (TLBIASID, TLBSYNC), _unmap clears the entries and
does the same before it returns. Step 23 (kgpu=23; with kgpu_keep: steps 1-21, 22 skipped, 23, then
kept) exercises them: 12 rounds of buffers of 16K to 4M made from scattered kernel pages, filled by
the 2D engine (step 22's fill, now at any address and pitch, its own stream unchanged), every row's
first and last pixel checked, then taken back; two buffers at once, the second one grain after the
first; the first's address unmapped and mapped onto the second's memory, filled again: the old
memory must stay as it was and the new one change (the TLB was told); a 34 MB buffer whose last 64K
need tables beyond the pool; one read-only entry's bits. Everything is freed in the step; the tables
made stay. Test: kgpu=23 kgpu_keep=1 kgpu_keep_s=120: "THE GPU'S OWN BUFFERS WORK", then kept and
undone as on #48.

